text.section:
Any of the following individuals may make a complaint to the Ombudsman with respect to a particular child, alleging that an administrative act is contrary to law, rule, or policy; imposed without an adequate statement of reason; or based on irrelevant, immaterial, or erroneous grounds:

The child, if the child is able to articulate a complaint, in accordance with the provisions of subsection A of § 2.2-446;


A biological parent of the child;


A foster parent of the child;


An adoptive parent or a prospective adoptive parent of the child;


A legally appointed guardian of the child;


A guardian ad litem for the child;


A relative of the child or any person with a legitimate interest as defined in § 20-124.1;


A Virginia legislator;


An individual required to report that a child is alleged to be an abused or neglected child under § 63.2-1509; and


An attorney for any individual described in subdivisions 1 through 7.
